{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789215431,"nonce":"7oMExhCFI+VAJH7zZuF7fE8GfPI=","title":"ZyntaxRuntime::finalize_runtime_symbols rebuilds without restoring","message":"The same hole a73f4d0 closed in the tiered runtime, in the classic one.\n`ZyntaxRuntime::finalize_runtime_symbols` calls\n`rebuild_with_accumulated_symbols` directly and recompiles nothing\nafterwards, so every module loaded before the call keeps its compiled\ncode and loses the addresses of its globals. A handler's op table is\none of those.\n\nThe tiered fix keeps every loaded module in load order and recompiles\nall of them after a rebuild; the classic runtime holds its backend\ndifferently and needs the same list. Reproduce with two load_module\ncalls separated by finalize_runtime_symbols and a handler declared in\nthe first: try_handler_push_info reports the op-table global was never\ndeclared to the backend.","files":null}]}